# {{name}}

A Hapto instrument: a sine for each note a MIDI keyboard plays, at a level
in dB. `Poly` gives each note one of its voices, and each voice renders by
its note's `Expression`, in which every bend and tuning a host sends is
already in the pitch.

- `cargo hapto dev` runs it as an app of its own while you edit it, played
  by every MIDI input the computer has. `cargo hapto dev --host` runs it
  through the dev host, in VST3 or the C interface, with a settings window of
  what the host sees.
- `cargo hapto build --install` lays out its VST3 bundle and installs it for
  the hosts on this machine; `cargo hapto validate` runs pluginval on it.
- `cargo hapto juce` writes `hapto-juce.cmake`, its settings for Hapto's JUCE
  adapter, and prints the CMake that builds it through JUCE: as AU, AAX or a
  JUCE VST3.
- `cargo test` drives it through the VST3 exporter, as a host does, and
  plays it with no host at several block sizes, which must sound the same.

Its identity is in `Cargo.toml`, under `[package.metadata.hapto]`: a host
knows the plugin by its ids for good, so they never change once it ships.
